## ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — NEVER HARDCODE VALUES
Always read from process.env. Key variables:
  DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASSWORD
  JWT_SECRET, JWT_EXPIRES_IN, BCRYPT_ROUNDS
  PORT, NODE_ENV, CLIENT_URL, SOCKET_CORS_ORIGIN
  AGENTROUTER_BASE_URL, AGENTROUTER_API_KEY, AI_MODEL
  STORAGE_DRIVER, UPLOAD_DIR

---

## TYPESCRIPT RULES
- No "any" type — always define proper interfaces in /types
- Always async/await — never raw .then() chains
- Named exports for services, controllers, middleware
- Default exports only for Express routers
- Every Sequelize model must have a TypeScript interface above it

---

## HOW TO RESPOND WHEN ASKED TO BUILD A FEATURE
1. State which files you will create or modify
2. Build in order: types → model → service → controller → route
3. Add ALL comments per the commenting rules above
4. End with the curl command to verify it works
5. End with the git commit command:
   git add . && git commit -m "feat: description of what was built"

